      "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn DeepSeek-V4.1 prefill, every TP rank runs the sparse-attention indexer (logits and top-k) for all rows of the chunk, so at TP4 three quarters of that work repeats on every rank. #42968 shards these rows across the TP ranks behind `SGLANG_OPT_DSV4_INDEXER_TP_SHARD`, but only in the CUDA backend (`deepseek_v4_backend.py` and `dsv4/v41_indexer`). The HIP backend's low-ratio indexer (`DeepseekV4HipRadixBackend._low_ratio_index_topk`, which calls `low_ratio_index_topk_hip_extend`) still scores every row on every rank. In our long-prompt benchmark on MI355X at TP4, the prefill indexer is about 8% of prefill kernel time.\n\nThis is a draft opened before the code, so the plan can be discussed first.\n\n## Modifications\n\nPlanned (no code in this draft yet):\n\n- Behind the same flag as #42968 (`SGLANG_OPT_DSV4_INDEXER_TP_SHARD`, off by default), the HIP prefill indexer scores `ceil(rows / tp)` rows on each rank and all-gathers the selected indices over the attention TP group, following #42968's `RowShard` and its minimum row count.\n- Decode and verify steps are unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot run yet. Plan: the selected top-k indices equal to the unsharded path for every layer kind, then GSM8K and long-context NIAH with the same server config, with and without the flag.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot run yet. Plan: indexer kernel time per prefill chunk, and long-prompt TTFT and output throughput at TP4 on MI355X, with and without speculative decoding.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [ ] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #41622666363](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41622666363)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41622665954](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41622665954)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.a